// Managed by the debian_microserver role.
// Package work yields CPU and disk to serving. dpkg, and every DKMS build it
// runs (such as zfs-dkms after a kernel update), inherits nice 19 and the idle
// I/O class from the APT process. A failed hook aborts APT, so failures are
// ignored: a slower update is acceptable, a blocked one is not.
DPkg::Pre-Invoke { "/usr/bin/renice -n 19 -p $PPID >/dev/null 2>&1 || true; /usr/bin/ionice -c 3 -p $PPID >/dev/null 2>&1 || true"; };
